<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40818" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-flŭo</span></b> ,
			ĕre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to flow</i> or <i>run back;</i>
			<i>to flow off</i>, <i>overflow</i>
				(<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Maeandros ambiguo lapsu refluitque fluitque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 163</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">refluit amnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 240</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8, 87</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. G. 4, 262</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nilus campis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					9, 32</span></i>
			. — 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Of the tide,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 97, 99, § 213</span></i>
			.</div>
